# The release commit's message. `npm version` writes it, `%s` is the new version,
# and the `v` is what makes it `v<version>` rather than `<version>` — the shape every
# release commit in this repository's history has, and the one the tag carries.
#
# It is here rather than in a global config because the release is one command
# (`npm version patch`) and this is the only place that command reads. There is
# nothing else in this file on purpose: `actions/setup-node` writes the registry
# and the auth token into its own `.npmrc` under `RUNNER_TEMP`, and a second copy
# of the scope here would be a second place for it to be wrong — the way it is
# wrong is a 401 that reads like a bad token.
message=v%s
